//
// The security boundary: chrome.webstorePrivate is reachable from an
// ordinary (non-extension) web page context and ONLY from the real Chrome
// Web Store origin -- matches chrome/common/extensions/api/
// _api_features.json's own "webstorePrivate" entry (minus its second,
// testing-only <all_urls> stanza, which exists for chrome/'s own
// webstore_override.cc and has no Orbit equivalent). Enforced twice: the
// renderer never installs the chrome.webstorePrivate binding into a context
// that doesn't match, and independently, ExtensionFunction::HasPermission()
// re-checks this same feature against the browser-verified committed URL of
// the calling RenderFrameHost before Run() ever executes -- so a compromised
// renderer cannot forge access by skipping the JS binding.

{
  "webstorePrivate": {
    "channel": "stable",
    "contexts": ["web_page"],
    "matches": ["https://chromewebstore.google.com/*"]
  }
}
